# 31. Success Criteria
The MVP is successful only if all of the following are demonstrated.

## SC-01
Telegram interactions generate real reply/convergence events.

## SC-02
Five-to-one convergence triggers analysis.

## SC-03
Maya and Chris receive different agent verdicts despite identical current messages and identical convergence topology.

## SC-04
The difference is caused by persistent historical context.

## SC-05
At least one intervention is executed through the live system.

## SC-06
The incident remains open after intervention.

## SC-07
A later process autonomously evaluates the incident.

## SC-08
The outcome is persisted back into agent context.

## SC-09
The dashboard visually communicates the difference within seconds.

## SC-10
The full demo can be understood within two minutes.

---

# 32. North-Star Hackathon Proof
The single most important technical proof is:

```
SAME CURRENT INPUT
+
DIFFERENT PERSISTENT HISTORY
=
DIFFERENT MIND DECISION
```
If this works reliably, TEMPER proves deep Minds integration.

If this does not work reliably, visual polish must not be prioritized over fixing it.

---

# 33. Evaluation Against Hackathon Criteria

## Minds Integration Depth
TEMPER relies on:

- persistent community history
- relationship context
- incident continuity
- intervention outcome memory
- autonomous follow-up
Memory directly changes the verdict.

Target score:

**10/10**

